{"assets":["/statement-assets/09fe943227d72235e274569b784f78abc99fb930333fea0493180f21d7e59d66.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"482","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Random Function and Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have a rooted tree consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices. Let's number them with integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" inclusive. The root of the tree is the vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". For each "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i > 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" direct parent of the vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":". We say that vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" is child for its direct parent "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have initially painted all the vertices with red color. You like to repaint some vertices of the tree. To perform painting you use the function "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"paint"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" that you call with the root of the tree as an argument. Here is the pseudocode of this function:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\ncount = 0 // global integer variable \n\nrnd() { // this function is used in paint code\n    return 0 or 1 equiprobably\n}\n\npaint(s) {\n    if (count is even) then paint s with white color\n    else paint s with black color\n\n    count = count + 1\n    \n    if rnd() = 1 then children = [array of vertex s children in ascending order of their numbers]\n    else children = [array of vertex s children in descending order of their numbers]\n\n    for child in children { // iterating over children array\n        if rnd() = 1 then paint(child) // calling paint recursively\n    }\n}\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As a result of this function, some vertices may change their colors to white or black and some of them may remain red."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to determine the number of distinct possible colorings of the vertices of the tree. We will assume that the coloring is possible if there is a nonzero probability to get this coloring with a single call of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"paint(1)"},{"kind":"text","text":". We assume that the colorings are different if there is a pair of vertices that are painted with different colors in these colorings. Since the required number may be very large, find its remainder of division by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of vertexes in the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p2, p3, ..., pn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ pi < i"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the parent of vertex "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the answer to the problem modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n1 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All possible coloring patterns of the first sample are given below."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/09fe943227d72235e274569b784f78abc99fb930333fea0493180f21d7e59d66.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"482D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/482/problem/D"}